import java.io.*;
import java.util.* ;

import java.util.ArrayList;

public class Solution {

	public static int LongestSubsetWithZeroSum(ArrayList<Integer> arr) {

		int n = arr.size();
		int maxi = 0;
		int sum = 0;
		Map<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();

		for(int i = 0; i < n; i++){
			sum += arr.get(i);

			if(sum == 0){
				maxi = i+1;
			}else{
				if(map.get(sum) != null){
					maxi = Math.max(maxi,i - map.get(sum));
				}else{
					map.put(sum,i);
				}
			}
		}
	return maxi;
		}
}


Ninja loves playing with numbers. So his friend gives him an array on his birthday. The array consists of positive and negative integers. Now Ninja is interested in finding the length of the
longest subarray whose sum is zero.


Example Input
arr = [1, -1, 2, -2, 3]

Expected Output
4


Because the longest zero-sum subarray is:

[1, -1, 2, -2]  → length = 4

🔁 Code Reminder (Important Part)
if (sum == 0) {
    maxi = i + 1;
}

