❓ Why exactly i + 1?

Because when:

sum == 0


It means:

arr[0] + arr[1] + ... + arr[i] = 0


So the subarray starts from index 0.

📏 Length formula:

end - start + 1
= i - 0 + 1
= i + 1

🧠 One-Line Memory Trick

If prefix sum becomes zero at index i, the zero-sum subarray starts from index 0, so its length is i + 1.

